THE COMMITTED BROWSER BUNDLE
============================

`public/app.js` and `public/app.css` are build artefacts, and they are committed
on purpose: the page that seals a player's number is part of what the freeze
commits to (docs/PROTOCOL.md §4.1), so it has to be in the tag a player is given.
That makes this repository a binary distribution of the seventeen libraries
compiled into that bundle — sixteen MIT, one BSD-3-Clause — and both of those
licences ask that their notices travel with such a distribution.

The bundle is built with `legalComments: 'none'`, so those notices live in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md instead. That file is regenerated on every build from
esbuild's own record of what went into the bundle, so it cannot fall behind a
dependency that was added later, and the build fails outright on a package whose
terms it cannot reproduce.

Everything else in this repository is original work under the licence above:
`generate.js`, every module under `server/`, `client/` and `tools/`, the
documents under `docs/`, and `data/schedule_template.json`. The runtime
dependency tree is one package.

`generate.js` and `data/schedule_template.json` in particular are meant to be
copied, re-run and argued with. Publishing them is the point.
